UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This is a good example of where the North hand is not nearly as good as its HCP indicates. The multitude of Queens and Jacks are overvalued and 4-3-3-3 distribution is terrible. |
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using Bergen evaluation it is worth 14 HCP, plus 1 quality suit point, less 2 points for 7 queens/jacks and no aces/tens. It is technically worth 13 barely a 1@C opener. But if North wanted to pass that would be okay as well.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As you see, despite having 23 HCP, we go down quite a bit in NT. We can barely make 3@C losing 4 aces assuming there is not diamond ruff.

|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


