UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let's discuss the best way to play the hand.|sk|n|pc|d4|at| On the surface, if declarer assumes a 2-1 heart break and draws 2 rounds of trumps he can count 10 tricks for sure--5 hearts in one hand, 3 ruffs, and 2 diamonds. That is only 10 tricks. But he needs an 11th.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|One possibility is to hope the @SA is onside but that is unlikely given the auction. The other possibility is to set up club tricks in dummy. The way I would have played the hand is to cash the @DA and @DK and discard 2 spades.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|sk||cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And then lead a club. If he then ruffs clubs 3 times declarer will take 12 tricks--2 diamonds, 3 ruffs, 5 hearts, and 2 clubs. So on the diamond lead he should make 6. Even on the heart lead he can make 6.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


