UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I could have opened 1NT. Bergen would because he counts my hand as 15 by adding one for the quality heart suit although, I am not a big fan of that. If I have less than 15 HCP, I only open 1N if my |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at| add up to 16 or more. |
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So if I have a quality 5 card suit and 14 HCP I would open 1N. But if you want to open 1N using purely starting point count of 15-17 that is very reasonable.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Had I opened 1N, North should bid 2@H transfer and then bid 4@H over my 2@S response to show 5-5. North, with hand, definitely should not bid |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| over a 1N opener because he wants to see if opener has a 3-card major and |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| will only discover a 4 card major. |
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although in theory he could bid Stayman, and if I bid 2@D he could jump to 3@S and if I bid 3N to deny 4 spades he could bid 4@H. But much more straight forward to just transfer and jump to 4@H.

|
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


